  "body": "Some mobile platforms show notifications on their lock-screen (prior to the user _logging in_), which is great for a quick peek about what's going on, but not so great for notifications that contain rather sensitive content. In these cases, an implementation could decide to display a more generic/anonymized version instead.\n\nHow about adding a `sensitive` (boolean) option, defaulting to false?\n\n@jakearchibald \n",
